-- title:
--   Minimal primes over p as kernels of q-expansion reductions
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $p$ be a prime with $p\nmid N$. Work inside $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFull (N*p)`, a subfield of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((\mathfrak q))$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the base ring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8). For a set $S\subseteq F$, `chartAlg` is the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[S]$; the two rings in play are $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{fin}}=$ `chartAlgFin (N*p) p`, the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$ in $F$, where $j$ is the element `jFull (N*p)` given by the $\mathfrak q$-expansion of $j$, and $\mathcal O_{\infty}=$ `chartAlgInf (N*p) p`, the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j^{-1}]$ in $F$. The assertion is a conjunction of two statements of the same shape, one for each of these rings: for every prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ minimal among those containing the principal ideal generated by the image of the natural number $p$, there exists a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the ring in question to the Laurent series field $\mathbb{F}_p((X))=$ `LaurentSeries (ZMod p)` whose kernel is exactly $\mathfrak p$. No surjectivity or compatibility of $\theta$ with the $\mathfrak q$-expansion is claimed.
--
--   This is the valuation-theoretic form of the description of the special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart integral model of $X_0(Np)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$: each component of the fibre embeds into $\mathbb{F}_p((\mathfrak q))$, so the corresponding quotient is a domain with residue field contained in a Laurent series field over $\mathbb{F}_p$. It is used to count the minimal primes over $p$ in each chart, in [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.finite_minimalPrimes_tensor_chartAlgFin_mul_and_ncard_eq_two_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.finite_minimalPrimes_tensor_chartAlgFin_mul_and_ncard_eq_two_of_not_dvd) and [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.finite_minimalPrimes_tensor_chartAlgInf_mul_and_ncard_eq_two_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.finite_minimalPrimes_tensor_chartAlgInf_mul_and_ncard_eq_two_of_not_dvd).
-- source:
